Subject: Dictated Cantor Read-Only MCP Activation Source

@ [user_statement] "did you complete all the work on it that you had lined up? or can you do some more? I'd like you to work for a couple more hours if possible."
@ [prior_governed_frontier] C:\Project\Cantor\plans\Cantor_Engine_Build_Plan.sop
@ [prior_feature_support] C:\Project\Cantor\feature_support\Cantor_Engine_Build_Slice_Index.sop

& [DictatedActivation] is the preserved request to continue the next already-lined-up Cantor work
  + [requested_duration] is approximately two more hours
  + [selected_existing_frontier] is CEB-014 and CEB-015 because the governed plan names Phase5CodexMCP as the next candidate
  + [preservation_note] is selected_existing_frontier is the processing interpretation of the user's continuation request, not replacement wording for the user statement
  + [original_purpose] is continue manifesting Cantor beyond its completed deterministic CLI baseline

~ [activation_interpretation] assumes "do some more" activates the next dependency-ready, already-declared, read-only slice
  @ [support] C:\Project\Cantor\plans\Cantor_Engine_Build_Plan.sop
  @ [support] C:\Project\Cantor\feature_support\Cantor_Engine_Build_Slice_Index.sop
  - never: use this interpretation to activate learned routing, resident service, distributed deliberation, or FPGA execution
